  "8d30a986-42e7-4010-9106-c3ddb0e65c5f": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p5-teaching",
     "replacement": "- If $P(\\alpha)=0$, then $P(x)=(x-\\alpha)Q(x)$, where $Q(x)$ is a polynomial.\n- If $P(\\alpha)=P'(\\alpha)=0$, then $P(x)=(x-\\alpha)^2Q(x)$.\n- If $P(\\alpha)=P'(\\alpha)=P''(\\alpha)=0$, then $P(x)=(x-\\alpha)^3Q(x)$.\n- In general, $P(\\alpha)=P'(\\alpha)=\\cdots=P^{(m-1)}(\\alpha)=0$ if and only if $P(x)=(x-\\alpha)^mQ(x)$. The **multiplicity** of $\\alpha$ is exactly $m$ when also $P^{(m)}(\\alpha)\\ne0$.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p5-teaching",
     "targetFingerprint": "d2159990a53cb50318cbde2dc7bfc49b73b573cbb4401f43a91a22cab4757875",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6ext1-1-multiplicity-of-zeroes-of-polynomial-functions-v1/20261111-091733",
   "revision": 13
  },
  "39b493c1-9ff1-4de6-a7e5-6b2923a5caef": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p7-method",
     "replacement": "1. Test the factors of the constant term, divided by the factors of the leading coefficient, to find a zero.\n2. Test each zero in $P'(x)$ and $P''(x)$ to find its multiplicity.\n3. Use the sum and product of zeroes, counting each zero as many times as its multiplicity, to find the other zeroes.\n  A polynomial of degree $n$ has at most $n$ zeroes, counted with multiplicity.\n4. As a last resort, multiply the known linear factors together and use long division.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p7-method",
     "targetFingerprint": "8ad227057ea0690c15e9b3c72f1611281d5965d599be9cc76995655dafc1bd8d",
     "applied": true
    }
